    id: '19',
    title: 'Tunisia Africa Business Meetings 2024: KASCOTE Expands Trade Horizons in North Africa',
    excerpt: 'KASCOTE participated in the 3rd Tunisia Africa Business Meetings (TABM) in Tunis, engaging with over 250 Tunisian exporters and 100+ African buyers to explore bilateral trade opportunities across key sectors.',
    content: 'KASCOTE delegation participated in the 3rd Tunisia Africa Business Meetings (TABM), held on July 2-3, 2024, in Tunis, Tunisia. This prestigious international trade event provided an exceptional platform for African traders and entrepreneurs to connect with Tunisian exporters and explore business partnerships across diverse sectors.\n\nEvent Overview\n\nTunisia Africa Business Meetings (TABM) Significance\n- Premier African-Tunisian business networking platform\n- Held in partnership with Arab Africa Trade Bridges (AATB) Program\n- Supported by German Agency for International Cooperation (GIZ)\n- Strategic event for enhancing Sub-Saharan Africa-Tunisia trade\n- 3rd edition showcasing growing momentum in Africa-Tunisia relations\n\nEvent Participants\n- Approximately 250 Tunisian exporting firms\n- Over 100 African buyers from 30 countries\n- Government officials and trade promotion agencies\n- Industry leaders and business associations\n- International trade and investment organizations\n\nMarket Context\n\nTunisia-Sub-Saharan Africa Trade Growth\n- 2023 bilateral trade reached $650 million\n- Tunisian exports exceeded $490 million\n- Growing momentum in Africa-Tunisia commercial relations\n- Expanding opportunities across multiple sectors\n- Strategic importance for African market development\n\nKey Industries Represented\n\n1. Agri-Food Sector - Agricultural products, food processing, spices, organic foods\n2. Pharmaceutical Industry - Medicines, healthcare solutions, quality standards\n3. Textiles and Clothing - Garment manufacturing, textiles, fashion apparel\n4. Mechanical and Electrical Industries - Machinery, equipment, components\n5. Additional Sectors - Leather goods, construction materials, IT services\n\nKASCOTE Participation Highlights\n\nBusiness Networking and Strategic Outcomes achieved through TABM 2024 participation with multiple business connections, market opportunities identified, and trade partnership frameworks established.',
