    title: 'Trade Mission to Sanabel Carthage: Exploring Cereal-Based Food Products Partnership',
    excerpt: 'KASCOTE visited Sanabel Carthage, a leading Tunisian brand specializing in high-quality cereal-based food products, led by President Alhaji Hassan Tahir Yaro to explore business and partnership opportunities.',
    content: 'KASCOTE undertook a trade mission to Sanabel Carthage in Tunisia, led by President Alhaji Hassan Tahir Yaro. Sanabel Carthage is a prominent Tunisian brand specializing in the production of high-quality cereal-based food products, operating as part of the SMID Group (Société des Minoteries et des Industries Diverses).\n\nAbout Sanabel Carthage and SMID Group\n\nSanabel Carthage is renowned for its expertise in cereal-based food manufacturing and quality production standards. The parent company, SMID Group, has been a major player in the Tunisian milling and food processing industry since 1992, with extensive experience in producing nutritious and quality food products.\n\nMission Objectives\n\nThe delegation visited to: explore product quality and manufacturing processes, identify import-export opportunities for Nigerian markets, discuss partnership and distribution arrangements, learn about food safety and quality standards. The visit facilitated direct engagement with Sanabel Carthage leadership.\n\nBusiness Outcomes\n\nThe trade mission enabled KASCOTE members to: understand cereal-based product sourcing, evaluate supply chain integration opportunities, explore market entry strategies in Tunisia, establish direct contacts with Sanabel Carthage management.',
